<title>LATVIA: LATVIA-RUSSIAN, LATVIAN TRANSPORT OFFICIALS TO MEET.</title>
<headline>LATVIA-RUSSIAN, LATVIAN TRANSPORT OFFICIALS TO MEET.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Transport Minister Vilis Krishtopans on Thursday headed to Moscow as leader of a delegation of transport officials which will discuss air links and aviation company debts.</p>
<p>Latvia has for some time been trying to convince Russia to allow a second Latvian airline, Air Baltic, to fly between Riga and Moscow. To this end, Latvia recently paid a debt it owed to Moscow airport for landing rights.</p>
<p>The officials will also discuss freight and customs issues, the transport ministry said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
